cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "ScamEncyclopedia open data: regulator warning lists, scam taxonomy, fraud statistics"
authors:
  - name: "ScamEncyclopedia"
    website: "https://scamencyclopedia.org"
    email: "hello@scamencyclopedia.org"
url: "https://scamencyclopedia.org/data"
repository-code: "https://github.com/bryanflowers/scamencyclopedia-data"
license: "CC-BY-4.0"
notes: >-
  This dataset is dual-licensed. The regulator-warnings.csv and regulator-warnings.json files
  are licensed CC-BY-NC-4.0 (not CC-BY-4.0) because they carry OpenSanctions-structured rows
  under OpenSanctions' own CC-BY-NC 4.0 terms. All other files are CC-BY-4.0. See LICENSE.md.
date-released: "2026-09-12"
version: "2026-09-12"
keywords:
  - fraud
  - scams
  - regulator-warnings
  - consumer-protection
  - open-data
  - osint
abstract: >-
  Open datasets published by ScamEncyclopedia: 11,041 regulator warning-list entries structured
  via OpenSanctions from 8 official regulators (US SEC, Swiss FINMA, Securities Commission
  Malaysia, France AMF, Philippines SEC, Malaysia Financial Consumer Alert List, Lithuania
  illegal financial services, and Lithuania Gaming Control Authority), a scam taxonomy of
  roughly 960 scam sub-types (959 at the September 2026 snapshot), cited fraud statistics with named sources, and aggregate counts
  from public threat feeds. Refreshed weekly.
